Frontend (Client-Side)

What users see and interact with in the browser.

Built with HTML, CSS, JavaScript.

Focus: layout, styles, usability, responsiveness.

Real-world example:
The visible parts of Amazon—product images, search bar, “Add to Cart” button.

Backend (Server-Side)

Handles logic, authentication, databases, APIs.

Built with Node.js, Java, Python, PHP, etc.

Focus: processing requests, storing/retrieving data, executing logic.

Real-world example:
When you order food on Swiggy, the backend processes your login, order details, payments, etc.

Full-Stack

Developer who works on both frontend and backend.

Builds user interface, server logic, and database.

Real-world example:
A developer who creates both the login page and the actual login verification system behind it.
